{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"length"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5Int32V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int32"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","title":"length","externalID":"s:6Yorkie0A19_V1_TreeRestoreSpanV6lengths5Int32Vvp","modules":[{"name":"Yorkie"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan\/length"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan\/length"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"length"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int32","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5Int32V"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"set"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan":{"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"TreeRestoreSpan carries a tree node run from a single deletion, addressed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by TreeNodeID identity, for identity-preserving Tree undo\/redo. Unlike the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text RestoreSpan (flat offsets), a tree span records the node’s structure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(type\/attrs) and its position anchors, because in a tree id-order is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sibling-order: left_sibling_id and right_sibling_id are redundant external"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary anchors of the deleted run, so restore can reconstruct the run’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal order from the op’s own spans and needs only one surviving"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary to place it. value\/attributes are a deep copy so a GC-purged node"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be recreated."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan/length":{"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan\/length","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"length","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int32","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5Int32V"}],"role":"symbol","title":"length","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan\/length","kind":"symbol","abstract":[]},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie","title":"Yorkie","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie"}}}